ratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 50 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.450 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El hecho de que se adjudiquen contratos cerca del límite no implica que haya sido un error. Puede deberse a razones como precios de mercado o necesidades específicas.\nQué se puede revisar: Es importante comprobar cuántos contratos se adjudicaron en diciembre y si algunos atienden la misma necesidad. También se debe revisar qué pasó con el adjudicatario A en el último año.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 67 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 13.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.1, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.6 to 7.2. Contract [1], for 14,450 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: a pile-up of amounts just under the limit is a statistical indicator. It does not prove that any contract was broken up or that anyone acted improperly; it may reflect market prices, fixed budgets or separate needs.\nWhat can be checked: in the linked contract files, what was bought in each case and on which dates, and whether several contracts meet a single need that could have been procured at once.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"plantilla","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["JevHxwkfjl6TylGzYmBF9Q%3D%3D","ZaPMFgolhSRSYrkJkLlFdw%3D%3D","L6PnVHKR5dmFQ%2FlhRK79lA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}